Third-party protocol assets
---------------------------

The files under protos/ are copied without modification from
https://github.com/teslamotors/fleet-telemetry
commit bb7c8a931e46da3b3eb6d20a67541c8f755f1ee6
(2026-11-03, "Add SelfDrivingSoftwareVersion and SemiTrailerLatched fields").

Those files are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Copyright Tesla Motors, Inc. and the contributors of that repository.
The Apache License text ships with this crate as LICENSE-APACHE and in the
upstream repository.

The PEM bundles certs/prod_ca.crt and certs/eng_ca.crt are copied from
config/files/ in the same commit. They are the client-certificate CA chains
the reference server loads in ExtractServiceTLSConfig (config/config.go).
They are public certificates, not private keys.

The FlatBuffers envelope in src/envelope.rs is reconstructed from the
generated Go under messages/tesla/ in that same commit
(FlatbuffersEnvelope.go, FlatbuffersStream.go, FlatbuffersStreamAck.go,
Message.go, and flatbuffers_extension.go). The upstream repository does not
publish the .fbs source. The module documentation on `envelope` records the
reconstructed schema, including the ack-encoding quirk.
